<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n71344" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νύχιος</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῠ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ος</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			E.
			<u>IT</u>
			1273
		</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
			Tim.
			<u>Fr.</u>
		</span></i>II, parodied by <i><span class="en">
			Macho
		</span></i> ap.<i><span class="en">
			Ath.
			8.341d
		</span></i> :—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>nightly,</i> i.e. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> of persons, <i>doing</i> a thing <i>by night,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. καταλέξεται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					523
				</span></i>
			 (v.l.), cf.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Th.</u>
				991
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				588
			</span></i>, etc. ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνὴρ δ᾽ ἐκτέταται ν.</span>”
				<i>as in nightly sleep,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					857
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>belonging to night,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. φθέγματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ant.</u>
					1147
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.) ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνοπαί, γόοι,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IT</u>
				1277
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>El.</u>
				141
			</span></i> (both lyr.) : in late Prose, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. θεός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dam.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					273
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> of places,
				<i>dark as night, gloomy,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νυχίαν πλάκα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					953
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.) ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δι᾽ ἅλα ν.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Med.</u>
					211
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.) ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄντρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Andr.</u>
					1224
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.) ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ μέλαθρα
			νύχια,</span> i.e. into the nether world, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Hel.</u>
				177
			</span></i> (lyr.) ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χάος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Av.</u>
					698
				</span></i>
			 : in later Prose, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ τῶν ἄντρων ν.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Porph.
					<u>Antr.</u>
					9
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
